{"nas": [{"id": "naS", "headword": "नश्", "headword_slp1": "naS", "fold": "nas", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "1 नश् न॑श्यति (˚ते) &\nन॑शति (˚ते), pp. नष्ट॑ (q.v.) be lost or missing, vanish,\ndisappear, wane, perish, fly, escape, be gone. C. नाश॑यति (˚ते),\npp. नाशित make disappear, expel, destroy, violate, deflower;\n lose,\nalso from memory, i.e. forget. — अप be gone. अव wane, disappear.\nनिस् C. expel, drive away. प्र (णश्यति) be lost, disappear, run\naway. विप्र be lost, vanish, have no effect or result. संप्र\ndisappear, cease. वि be lost, vanish, perish, have no effect or\nsuccess;\n be deprived of (abl.). C. make disappear, destroy, annihilate,\nkill. अनुवि disappear or perish after (acc.). — Cf. प्रनष्ट,\nविनष्ट, विप्रनष्ट.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2 नश् (नंश्), न॑शति, ˚ते attain, get, meet with\n(loc.);\n reach, befall. D. इ॑नक्षति q.v. — अच्छ come near. अभि,\nउद्, परि, प्र, वि & सम् reach, attain.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "nas", "headword": "नस्", "headword_slp1": "nas", "fold": "nas", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "1 नस् न॑सते meet, encounter;\n copulate (man and wife).\n—सम् meet, join with (instr.).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2 न॑स् f. nose (only नसा॑, नसि॑, नसो॑स्, नस्त॑स्, & adj.\n—˚).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "3 नस् (encl.) us, to us, or of us (acc., dat., & gen. pl. of\n1st pers. pron).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "nasana": [{"id": "naSana", "headword": "नशन", "headword_slp1": "naSana", "fold": "nasana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "नशन n. disappearance, loss.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "nASana", "headword": "नाशन", "headword_slp1": "nASana", "fold": "nasana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "ना॑शन f. ई destroying, removing (gen. or —˚);\n n. as\nsubst.", "gloss_lang